        "Place a wire rack over the coals, add the meat, and cook until it has a little singe and color.",
        "To ensure equal cooking on all sides, turn meat frequently.",
        "Use a fresh brush and some oil or marinade to flavor the meat and keep it from drying out while it cooks.",
        "To allow the inside of the meat to cook slowly and effectively, wrap it in a packet of foil. Or, keep grilling until the food is done to the liking.",
        "Once the meat is done, use a sharp knife to cut it into bite-sized pieces.",
        "Serve."
